// Title: ClickOnce Deployment Execution - Dfsvc.EXE Child Process
// Sigma ID: 241d52b5-eee0-49d0-ac8a-8b9c15c7221c
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-06-12 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects child processes of "dfsvc" which indicates a ClickOnce deployment execution.
// False positives:
//   - False positives are expected in environement leveraging ClickOnce deployments. An initial baselining is required before using this rule in production.
// References:
//   - https://posts.specterops.io/less-smartscreen-more-caffeine-ab-using-clickonce-for-trusted-code-execution-1446ea8051c5
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_dfsvc_child_processes.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\dfsvc.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\AppData\\Local\\Apps\\2.0\\"
